{"availability":"available","full":"technologylab-ai/omagma","name":"omagma","description":"A compact read-only Gmail dropdown for the Omarchy bar, with separate accounts and Chrome profiles.","category":"Other","language":"Zig","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-04T20:19:03Z","updated":"2026-10-09T19:15:01Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://technologylab-ai.github.io/omagma/","topics":[],"demo":"https://technologylab-ai.github.io/omagma/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T19:34:19.606Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T19:34:19.606Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T19:34:19.606Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T19:34:19.606Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Gmail in the Omarchy bar, your Linux or Mac terminal, and agent workflows. Keep up to three accounts separate, check recent mail without a browser tab, and open Gmail in each account’s configured Chrome profile.","The compact bar dropdown shows each account’s unread count, sender, subject, time and message snippet. It keeps up to 30 recent Inbox messages per account in memory, with optional five-minute background refresh. The bar is read-only and does not save mail to disk.","Omagma started because one Gmail tab was using roughly 2 GB of RAM on the author’s desktop. On 2026-10-05, Omagma’s backend and attributed UI share measured approximately 31 MB for three connected accounts in v0.2.2 on Linux x8664. Chrome and unrelated shell widgets are excluded. These are approximate observations, not a controlled browser benchmark. Memory details."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/technologylab-ai/omagma/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"920973be74bb27543326ecffc582c67c28b3ab29aee6e7233174c109cc50c830","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T19:34:19.706Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T19:34:19.706Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Gmail in the Omarchy bar, your Linux or Mac terminal, and agent workflows. Keep up to three accounts separate, check recent mail without a browser tab, and open Gmail in each account’s configured Chrome profile.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/technologylab-ai/omagma/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"not_required","text":"It provides separate accounts, full mail and threads, a reader beside or below the list, Vim keys, mouse navigation, native HTML-to-text display, search, local drafts, replies/forwarding, contacts, custom labels, attachments, mailbox changes and invitation replies. $EDITOR takes over the terminal and returns to the draft; tmux is not required.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/technologylab-ai/omagma/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"920973be74bb27543326ecffc582c67c28b3ab29aee6e7233174c109cc50c830","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/technologylab-ai/omagma/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T19:34:19.706Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-09T19:15:01Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/technologylab-ai/omagma/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T19:34:19.706Z","hash":"920973be74bb27543326ecffc582c67c28b3ab29aee6e7233174c109cc50c830","originalBytes":11036,"storedBytes":11036,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["docs","omagma","mail","account","bar","tui","linux","terminal","cli","accounts","cache","google","images","preview","chrome","installation","omarchy","separate","agent","available","background","choose","complete","contacts","each","gmail","install","keep","markdown","message","one","open","private","release","setup","zig","changes","compact","draft","files","follow","mac","memory","new","opens","optional","read-only","source","through","while","access.","backend","builds","cached","card","checks","credentials","documentation","download","drafts","dropdown","explicit","features.md","fictional","fixtures","guide","homebrew","inbox","install.md","keeps","keys","labels","limit","links","macos","macos.md"